# Page rewrite map

Rewrite copy inside the existing JSX only. Section order and components stay as-is; if the current section order fights the message, flag it — don't restructure.

## Home (`/`)

Hero: buyer-facing. One line that says what RidgeRise sells (qualified inbound calls, leads, and traffic in high-intent verticals) and one line on how (in-house media buying plus a screened publisher layer, CPL and pay-per-call models). Primary CTA → `/buyers` or `/contact`.
Body sections: verticals showcase (buyer framing), how it works for buyers, quality/compliance approach, then ONE publisher section near the bottom with CTA → `/publishers`. Publisher content never appears above buyer content.
Tagline in `src/data/site.ts` may be rewritten to a buyer-slanted line if the user approves — propose options first.

## Buyers (`/buyers`) — the money page

Must cover, in the reader's order of concern:
1. What they can buy: exclusive/shared inbound calls, live transfers, CPL leads, qualified traffic.
2. Pricing models: cost per call (pay per call) and CPL, plus traffic deals — explained in one plain paragraph each, no jargon walls.
3. Where volume comes from: we buy the media ourselves, then add a screened publisher layer when in-house cannot carry the volume.
4. Quality controls: qualification before transfer, duration rules, tracking, source-level monitoring, dispute handling — described as practices, no invented numbers.
5. Filters they control: vertical, geo, schedule, concurrency, exclusivity.
6. Verticals list linking to `/verticals/{slug}`.
7. CTA: start a test campaign / get vertical pricing.

## Publishers (`/publishers`)

Shorter and denser than Buyers. Cover: live buyer demand across listed verticals, accepted traffic types, quality standards, tracking transparency, payout reliability (no invented payout numbers or cycles — placeholder if needed), application CTA. Tone: selective partner program, not an open affiliate signup.

## Verticals hub + detail

Hub intro frames verticals as "where we have buyer demand and campaign supply." Detail pages follow 50-verticals-content.mdc.

## About

Story of the model, not a founder biography with invented history. Why hybrid supply, why call-first, why quality obsession — written concretely. No fake years/team/office claims.

## Contact

Split the ask: buyers → "tell us your vertical, states, hours, and what a qualified call looks like"; publishers → "tell us your traffic type and verticals." Keep forms/markup untouched.

## Privacy / Terms

Do not rewrite legal pages unless explicitly asked.
